angerous to discard because someone might be waiting for it for edge wait? But given discards, no indication.  \n\nI think W3 is slightly safer because W4 has been discarded, reducing the chance of someone needing W3 for W2-W3-W4.  \n\nSo I'll play W3.  \n\nAnswer: Play W3.  \n\nFinal output:  \n\nEvaluation: My hand is still far from ready, with many isolated tiles. I need to discard a tile that is safe and does not break promising sequences. The weakest tile is W3, as it is isolated and requires a specific W4 to form a chow, while other tiles like T3-T4-T5 and B5-B6 have more potential. Keeping F2 is valuable for potential double wind points.  \nReason: W3 is the most isolated and least useful for forming melds given current hand composition and visible discards. Discarding it maintains flexibility for other chows and avoids discarding more connected tiles.  \nAnswer: Play W3"}
